API.md §5.7: a let that names itself, directly or through another let, is no list of enum member
names, so the refinements over a, c and the two-let cycle give no finding and the lint terminates.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- m/m.canon --
package m

enum Color { red }

let a: [String] = [n for n in b]

let b: [String] = [n for n in a]

let c: [String] = c + [x.name for x in Color.members]

type T = String where it in a

type U = String where it in c
-- findings.txt --
0 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
